		{"id":"exegesis","type":"text","text":"## Scripture · [passage / source version]\nText in context · argument · structure · words · questions\n\nLink actual Scripture and Notion/source notes. Distinguish observation from interpretation.","x":30,"y":70,"width":560,"height":330,"color":"#4A90D9"},
		{"id":"synthesis","type":"text","text":"## Theology · [central claim]\nConnect the exegesis to Christ and the biblical story.\n\nAttribute research contributions by author/edition/page; name disputed or unresolved claims.","x":710,"y":70,"width":560,"height":330,"color":"#9B72CF"},
		{"id":"formation","type":"text","text":"## Formation · [Collective / goal]\nBelonging · Beholding · Becoming\n\nFor Collectives: develop separate Men’s/Women’s goals with actual pastoral rationale. Connect them to the text and synthesis; do not assume identical applications.","x":1390,"y":70,"width":560,"height":330,"color":"#65A86B"},
		{"id":"design","type":"text","text":"## Teaching Flow · [gathering / date]\nCollectives: two blocks, each 20 teaching + 10 discussion, inside a 6:30–8:00 PM gathering.\n\n20 community + 60 study + 10 closing. Provisional; adjust after use.\n\nLink this audience’s separate master. Planted can retain its own movements.","x":2070,"y":70,"width":560,"height":330,"color":"#D6B34B"},
		{"id":"discussion","type":"text","text":"## Discussion · [block / question]\nGalatians For You: primary development/question source. Traveling Light: secondary for freedom.\n\nRecord actual source edition/page, adaptation, formation goal, question intent, and optional leader cue.","x":2070,"y":460,"width":560,"height":300,"color":"#D96B6B"},
